.nh
.TH podman-system-renumber 1
.SH "نام (NAME)"
podman-system-renumber \- Migrate lock numbers to handle a change in maximum number of locks

.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBpodman system renumber\fP

.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\fBpodman system renumber\fP renumbers locks used by containers and pods.

.PP
Each Podman container and pod is allocated a lock at creation time, up to a maximum number controlled by the \fBnum_locks\fP parameter in \fBcontainers.conf\fP\&.

.PP
When all available locks are exhausted, no further containers and pods can be created until some existing containers and pods are removed. This can be avoided by increasing the number of locks available via modifying \fBcontainers.conf\fP and subsequently running \fBpodman system renumber\fP to prepare the new locks (and reallocate lock numbers to fit the new struct).

.PP
\fBpodman system renumber\fP must be called after any changes to \fBnum_locks\fP - failure to do so results in errors starting Podman as the number of locks available conflicts with the configured number of locks.

.PP
\fBpodman system renumber\fP can also be used to migrate 1.0 and earlier versions of Podman, which used a different locking scheme, to the new locking model. It is not strictly required to do this, but it is highly recommended to do so as deadlocks can occur otherwise.

.PP
If possible, avoid calling \fBpodman system renumber\fP while there are other Podman processes running.

.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
Renumber container and pod locks after modifying the num_locks setting in containers.conf.

.EX
$ podman system renumber
.EE

.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBpodman(1)\fP, \fBpodman-system(1)\fP, \fBcontainers.conf(5)\fP

.SH "تاریخچه (HISTORY)"
